        "biography": "Mary McLaglen, the daughter of Andrew McLaglen, is a producer and unit production manager who has contributed to a number of critically and financially successful motion pictures. Her career started on her father's North Sea Hijack (1979) as a production coordinator. She went on to work as a unit production manager on films like My Cousin Vinny (1992), Hope Floats (1998), Pay It Forward (2000), Two Weeks Notice (2002), Divine Secrets of the Ya-Ya Sisterhood (2002), Dodgeball (2004), Miss Congeniality 2 (2005), The Proposal (2009), Reel Steel (2011), The Internship (2013), and Deadpool & Wolverine (2024).",
